          "tool_use_id": "toolu_01CpQoeWozuZQcn1ZaEtyvzk",
          "tool_name": "write_file",
          "input_json": "{\u0022path\u0022:\u0022concepts/rag-hallucination-elimination-claim.md\u0022,\u0022content\u0022:\u0022---\\ntype: Concept\\ntitle: RAG hallucination elimination claim (marketing accuracy)\\ndescription: Examination of the common but inaccurate marketing claim that RAG systems eliminate hallucination entirely.\\ntimestamp: 2026-07-14T00:00:00Z\\ntags:\\n  - concept/RAG-Marketing-Claims\\n  - concept/Hallucination\\n  - concept/Marketing-Accuracy\\nconfidence: medium\\nconfidence_reason: \\u0022Single authoritative source identifying a specific, documented marketing claim pattern; corroboration would strengthen confidence.\\u0022\\n---\\n\\n## Overview\\n\\nMarketing materials for retrieval-augmented generation (RAG) products frequently make the claim that RAG systems \\u0022eliminate hallucination entirely.\\u0022 This claim is **not accurate**.\\n\\n## Why the claim is inaccurate\\n\\nWhile RAG does reduce hallucination compared to a pure parametric model by conditioning the generator\\u0027s response on retrieved documents, it does not eliminate hallucination because **retrieval quality caps answer quality**: a generator cannot produce a well-grounded answer if the retrieved context is irrelevant or incomplete.\\n\\nHallucination can still occur in RAG systems when:\\n- The retriever fails to fetch relevant documents\\n- Retrieved documents contain incorrect or conflicting information\\n- The generator misinterprets or conflates information from the retrieved context\\n- The retrieved documents do not cover the query\\u0027s topic\\n\\n## Relationship to retrieval quality\\n\\nThe effectiveness of a RAG system is fundamentally constrained by its retriever. No generator can overcome poor retrieval; therefore, a well-founded answer is impossible when retrieval itself fails. This is a structural limitation of RAG architectures, not a minor edge case.\\n\\n## Citations\\n\\n[^1]: Evaluation of RAG marketing claims and hallucination reduction (eval://steering-adoption/sample-01)\\n\\n\u0022}"
        }
      ],
